  "note": "Strict227 TDRP-R9-MICROTEX-RES-CYRILLIC-WNBX10-XML-PROVENANCE-001: res/cyrillic/wnbx10.xml@3e42b024a4d96f96a650babd183e58c31a02d31a is 25643 bytes/616 lines; Font root binds name=wnbx10.ttf, id=wnbx10, space=0.383331, xHeight=0.444445, quad=1.149994, unicode=95, itVersion=wnbxti10, ssVersion=wnssbx10, ttVersion=wntt10. It contains exactly 95 Char/95 unique codes (171..1141), 416 Kern records (266 -0.031944, 117 -0.095833, 13 -0.127777, 19 -0.063889, 1 +0.031944), 36 Lig records, 13 nonzero-depth chars and 5 italic-correction chars. Exact-path history is root 17f3fc78 init only; the blob is unchanged at the pinned MicroTeX commit, so c154's WNBX10 TTF namespace rewrite did not rewrite XML metrics. Historical DefaultTeXFontParser consumes each Char width/height/depth/italic plus Kern/Lig, resolves style variants, builds the adjacent TTF path and FontInfo; FontInfo lazily Font::create(path). Accepted addTeXFontDescription throws ex_alphabet_registration, so this XML table is not registered and parser can fall through to external-font/TextRenderingAtom if an external mapping exists. RES_README and Meson retain standalone install; legacy latex.qrc lists the XML, but accepted tdesktop uses external_microtex_bundled.rcc/bundled.qrc, which explicitly excludes Cyrillic/Greek. README excludes res/cyrillic XML/fonts from the MIT blanket and subtree LICENSE is GPLv3 provenance. Counters unknown=16149 unread=16124 omitted=0 responsibilities=245. Parent ebb18439 exact-head TDRP 61/61, Rust 6/6, Official MCP 1/1. Receipt-head Actions required. Next res/cyrillic/wnbxti10.ttf@e85a2a442738554dc728a75546d10fd6fef419d1.",
